WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Meet Asha. Tomorrow, she plans to renew her driving licence. She thinks it will take one visit.

00:08.000 --> 00:22.000
But her address changed, a challan is pending, and one document shortens her middle name. That can mean three portals and another day away from work.

00:22.000 --> 00:36.000
Asha opens Raahi. Instead of choosing a department, she starts with one outcome: finish everything in one successful visit.

00:36.000 --> 00:50.000
She says it naturally: “My licence expires next month. I moved. Check my challans before I go.” That is all Raahi needs.

00:50.000 --> 01:04.000
RoadReady turns her sentence into one sequence: clear the challan, update the address, renew the licence, then visit the right RTO. Three journeys become one.

01:04.000 --> 01:22.000
Now comes the moment that changes Asha’s day. VisitTwin rehearses the visit. Counter one clears. At counter two—stop. Her names do not match. One workday, 28 kilometres, and eleven days for another slot.

01:22.000 --> 01:37.000
Raahi explains the mismatch. Asha approves one correction. It flows across every linked service, and VisitTwin runs again. One, two, three, four—every counter clears.

01:37.000 --> 01:52.000
Only now does Asha receive her RoadReady Pass. The QR proves what is ready and where she is going, without exposing her licence, address proof, or payment numbers.

01:52.000 --> 02:00.000
Asha leaves home certain. Raahi does not digitize the queue. It prevents the failed visit.
